d 'JOINTDIAG': module to perform joint and simultaneous diagnostic tests for time-series models
d
d	The diagnostic tests in routine use -- Jarque-Bera,
d Breusch-Pagan,    Breusch-Godfrey, RESET, Engle's ARCH LM -- each
d test one departure from    the classical assumptions while
d assuming the remaining assumptions hold.    Bera and Jarque
d (1982) named the two consequences: undertesting (a	significant
d AR statistic that is really a misspecified functional form)	
d and overtesting (four separate 5% tests whose true joint size is
d nearer    20%).    jointdiag implements the literature that
d addresses this. It provides	 eleven subcommands of tests that
d either detect several misspecifications    simultaneously, or
d remain valid in the presence of the misspecification	  not
d currently being tested. 
d
d KW: time series
d KW: joint tests
d KW: diagnostics
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261005
d
d Author:   Merwan Roudane, NA
d Support: email  merwanroudane920@@gmail.com
d
